WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:04.380
Catalysts. Electrochemistry. Process engineering.

2
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:09.080
Hi, I'm Ayush Suryawanshi, and my work sits right where these three meet.

3
00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:11.861
I'm a chemical engineer from IIT Madras,

4
00:00:11.861 --> 00:00:15.300
and right now I'm a Management Trainee at LOXIM Industries.

5
00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:16.670
Let me show you what I do.

6
00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:19.000
It starts with the catalyst.

7
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:20.504
For my master's thesis,

8
00:00:20.504 --> 00:00:23.619
I added bismuth to platinum to stop carbon monoxide

9
00:00:23.619 --> 00:00:26.000
poisoning it in formic acid fuel cells.

10
00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:30.980
At NTNU in Norway, when the synthesis proved unsafe to scale, I reworked it.

11
00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:33.260
Then I put it to the test.

12
00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.120
In three-electrode cells, I measure what a catalyst really does.

13
00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:43.337
My best one held on to nearly 93% of its current after an hour. Commercial platinum?

14
00:00:43.337 --> 00:00:44.070
About 58%.

15
00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:47.140
But a good catalyst is only half the story.

16
00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:51.737
In Norway, I also worked with industry partners on a boiler retrofit:

17
00:00:51.737 --> 00:00:55.010
kinetic models, equipment sizing, safety and cost.

18
00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.700
At LOXIM, it all came together.

19
00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.037
On a two-month project,

20
00:00:59.037 --> 00:01:02.207
I mapped where a dye plant's effluent-treatment cost goes,

21
00:01:02.207 --> 00:01:03.792
and compared electrochemical,

22
00:01:03.792 --> 00:01:06.580
membrane and crystallisation routes with suppliers.

23
00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:07.327
The outcome:

24
00:01:07.327 --> 00:01:11.222
a proposed treatment train that turns the waste salt into a product,

25
00:01:11.222 --> 00:01:14.200
at a modelled operating cost about two-thirds lower.

26
00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:18.400
I handed it over with a validation roadmap for the next stage of evaluation.

27
00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:20.920
So, what am I looking for next?

28
00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:24.442
Roles in process engineering and electrochemical technologies,

29
00:01:24.442 --> 00:01:27.410
from chemical plants to fuel cells and electrolysers.

30
00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:31.636
If your team needs a process engineer who also speaks electrochemistry,

31
00:01:31.636 --> 00:01:33.030
I'd love to hear from you.

32
00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:33.910
Let's talk.
